  "result": "Fixed: subcommands now pick up their own entry from the parent's `default_map`.\n\n- **Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`), a child context copied the parent's whole `default_map`. A subcommand's options were therefore looked up in the group-level map instead of under the subcommand's name. The fix is `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`.\n- **Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It checks that `{\"foo\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}` applies to the `foo` subcommand.\n- **Results:** the full suite passes.",
